<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/bohemond-i-of-antioch" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bohemond-i-of-antioch.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-9">9 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Bohemond's knights rout Radwan of Aleppo near Antioch</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">As the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusaders</a> besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemond-i-of-antioch">Bohemond of Taranto</a> gathered all the remaining horses and marched by night against a relief army led by Radwan, the Seljuq ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>. After several cavalry charges the knights routed it, forcing Radwan back to Aleppo.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemond-i-of-antioch">Bohemond of Taranto</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-2">2 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Crusaders are let into Antioch by night</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">On the night of 2 to 3 June, a tower commander named Firouz let Bohemond's men over the walls, ending a seven-month siege. The crusaders were themselves besieged in the city days later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mosul" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mosul.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-28">28 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Crusaders break out of Antioch and rout Kerbogha</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Besieged in the city they had just taken, and inspired by the supposed discovery of the Holy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lance">Lance</a>, the crusaders defeated the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerbogha">Kerbogha</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a>. The road to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> lay open.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lance">Lance</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
